invariant: INV-16
file: src/base64.c
catches: test/lint-wide-multiply.sh
reason: base64url_class tests its first range with an if, so whether a
  token's character is a capital letter decides which path runs. A token
  is a bearer credential, and its characters are secret. The class is the
  same, so no test sees it; the branch count does, on the two 64-bit
  specs, which compile base64.c@host under -DCH_JWS with a ceiling of
  zero (docs/decisions.md 221).

--- old
uint8_t base64url_class(uint8_t c) {
    uint32_t x = c;
    uint32_t upper = range_mask(x, 'A', 'Z');
--- new
uint8_t base64url_class(uint8_t c) {
    uint32_t x = c;
    if (x >= 'A' && x <= 'Z') {
        return (uint8_t)(x - 'A');
    }
    uint32_t upper = range_mask(x, 'A', 'Z');
